# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the sliced host-tier restore window (docs/prefix-store-hygiene.md "Sliced restore"; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the branch that carries the sliced restore and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed head that carries the sliced restore (tp4/tier-slice, or the ship-4 branch after the integrator merged it;
# sed -i 's/tp4-ship-4/<tag>/' *.env). The flag lives in files the image carries (qwen_prefix_registry.py, qwen_prefix_scheduler_patch.py, serving_prefill_admission.py): an image built before it ignores the two names and
# the arm reads NOT_EXERCISED (no "host tier restore slice on" line). This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# TS4 (TIMED, the ABAB's A repeat): TS2 again (the control-to-control floor of tier_concurrent_compare.py), profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4, plan
# tier-concurrent-timed. THE ABAB: TS2 control, TS3 sliced, TS4 control repeat, TS5 sliced repeat, every boot a fresh reset. THE CONTROL IS THE SHIP-4 CANDIDATE ITSELF
# (c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4: the host tier on, the restore whole, octo, Lever N, W2, engine reuse); the sliced arm is the SAME profile plus exactly
# QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_RESTORE_SLICE=512 and QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_RESTORE_SLICE_MS=200 (derived by the gate, no profile twin), so the only difference between the two boots is when the restore does
# its work. TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. TS2 and TS4 are the ship-4 pack's TC3 and TC5 run again
# on this image: where the same window already ran them on an image that carries this code, they stand in (the flag is byte-identical off). READ each: the plan verdict PASS (the stall budget
# is JUDGED: no seat waited longer than the Lever N decode gap floor, 8 s, between two tokens in any window), then the four together: python3 scripts/ci/tier_concurrent_compare.py <TS2
# results> <TS3 results> <TS4 results> <TS5 results> (A control, B sliced, C control repeat, D sliced repeat): exit 0 needs every seat IDENTICAL over its common tokens, the returning,
# long-prompt and cold-twin answers IDENTICAL across the two, no longest wait over the budget; it prints the round p50/p99 of each window and the sliced arm's p99 and longest wait against
# the control's (percent) with the control-to-control FLOOR. In the sliced arm the lines "host tier restore slice on blocks=512 ms=200" and "host tier restore req=... slices=N max_slice_ms=X
# held_steps=M" must be in the container log (else NOT_EXERCISED) and no "restore slice fell back" line. Then python3 scripts/ci/tier_stall_breakdown.py <container log> for each boot: the
# freeze phase by phase. ESTIMATE (nothing of this has run on a card; scripts/ci/tier_slice_model.py): the restore's own contribution to a seat's longest wait falls from about 1.1 s (T3:
# 0.96 s restore plus 0.14 s spill) to a slice (about 0.2 s) plus a round, the returning turn's first token comes about 1.5 s later (11 or 12 slices, a round between each); the returning
# request's own final prefill step and engine build (about 4.2 to 4.8 s, T3) are NOT sliced, so the seats' longest wait is expected near 5 s against about 6 s whole, inside the 8 s floor and
# NOT under 2 s. Unqualified: a measurement, never evidence. Estimate: 50 minutes. TELEMETRY: the prefix step has no sidecar.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=tier-concurrent-timed
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_BOX_MINUTES=90
